<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  What Android's backup and device transfer carry, decided rather than inherited (PLANNING.md §5).

  Tempo keeps no event of its own: the calendar is the reader's calendar app's, and travels
  with it (its account's sync, or its own backup). What is Tempo's is the reader's choices, so
  an allowlist of one file:

  - `files/datastore/settings.preferences_pb`: the appearance, the clock and date formats, which
    calendars the agenda shows (Phase 2).

  Left out by not being named: the widgets' looks (keyed by widget ids, which a restore renews),
  caches, and `no_backup`. A chosen calendar is kept by its
  account and name as well as its id (PLANNING.md §5), because a restored phone gives the same
  calendars new ids.

  The same list twice on purpose: `<cloud-backup>` is the copy Android sends to Google Drive,
  end-to-end encrypted with the phone's PIN, pattern or password since Android 9, and only if
  the reader turned backup on; `<device-transfer>` is the direct phone-to-phone move. Tempo
  sends neither itself and needs no permission for them: Android does the moving.

  NOT `android:allowBackup="false"`: on Android 12 and later some makers' phones still move the
  app's data in a device transfer anyway.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <include domain="file" path="datastore/settings.preferences_pb" />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <include domain="file" path="datastore/settings.preferences_pb" />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
